    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0371" n="1829" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p2/pg1829"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">293.1111/10–851: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Indonesia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cochran</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Djakarta</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-10-08T14:00:00+07:30">October 8, 1951—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>534. Reply dated Sept 27 read from Indo FonOff Oct 6 to Emb note Sept 1 conveying
                    msg contained Depcirtel 220.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d207-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p> FonMin replied that upon serious consideration US request, Indo Govt prepared
                    support any collective measures taken by reps foreign powers at Peiping in favor
                    US Govt for purpose assisting Amer nationals mentioned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cochran</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
